{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/579756-thoughts-on-the-cover-mechanic-in-a-larp-setting","id":579756,"title":"Thoughts on the Cover Mechanic in a LARP setting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-05T06:48:18-07:00","id":579756,"title":"Thoughts on the Cover Mechanic in a LARP setting?","content":"So, long story short I'm planning to start running a NWoD Demon LARP at one point. For the most part, it shouldn't be any more difficult to run than Requiem/Requiem 2.0, Changeling, Mage or Hunter (All of which I've played in or ST'd Larp for at some point).<br /> <br /> The only potential really sticky point I'm getting at the planning phase is cover and the considerations for people who like dressing up in character for immersion - constantly swapping costumes as players change covers can be quite a tough proposition, but Demon revolves very thoroughly around the use of covers and their impact on gameplay.<br /> <br /> I'm almost definitely going to use the &quot;Simplified Cover&quot; rules, because otherwise it gets too messy for even a LARP, but I'm not sure how to handle the multiple covers thing. It might not even be an immediate concern: Your average starting PC will only have one cover regardless.<br /> <br /> So I'm really just throwing out for advice in terms of management to make it a bit more organic for people who'll want to costume without driving everyone mad from fiddliness! I'd like to leave it as intact as possible, but I want to apply the KISS rule to the situation. The cover system is great for stories, so I don't want to lose that at all.<br /> <br /> (cross posted on <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?760410-NWoD-Demon-Thoughts-on-the-Cover-Mechanic-in-a-LARP-setting\" target=\"_blank\">RPG.net Forums</a>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 07-05-2015, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T10:56:19-07:00","id":579978,"title":"","content":"Well, the I'd like to point out that, while a lot of people have multiple Covers, the vast majority of the time? I've found that players have one Cover that they keep for the vast majority of interactions. So, perhaps a bit of focus on the main cover is best.<br /> <br /> Then? Hats. It might be easiest if you use swapping hats out for different covers, and just keep the clothes on for your main covers. <br /> <br /> I don't know, I don't LARP, but that's my initial thought on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T16:18:58-07:00","id":580331,"title":"","content":"Name tag holders.<br /> <br /> As you swap covers you swap the card in the name tag holder. The name tag should have a brief physical description in addition to the name. We had a thread or two on this, let me look for them...<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/172421-demon-the-descent-larp\">found it</a>. Warning, it gets a little tangenty, but there are a few gems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 07-05-2015, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T18:14:27-07:00","id":580417,"title":"","content":"MCN: Yep, definitely. Until a Demon hits Primum 2/3 they're only going to be able to hold one cover, but spending the extra merit dots at character generation is an option that remains on the table. It's more a longer term consideration for when people build up a set of covers, get their primum up and whatnot. There's obviously also the use of Fa\u00e7ades, which is available at Primum 1, but that requires taking up cover exp in play. It's mostly just that setting it up so it's as clear as possible right off the bat. LARP tends to have a lot of conveniences/contrivances just to make things work more cleanly, really.<br /> <br /> Agentwestmer: I actually had a discussion with my wife yesterday about the same issues and she came up with a similar (if probably more visually elegant!) solution to that particular issue. It's a good idea/thread though.<br /> <br /> The idea would be to use A5/A6 sized Lanyards with sleeves which use an actual image of the cover (with the players dressing as their demons themselves). Swapping your cover would basically just involve either flipping your lanyard over (if you have two covers) or swapping the Lanyard you're wearing (for 3+). That way there's the automatic visual recognition without having to stare at a blob of text on someone's nametag. You could even use small clips or whatever attached to the Lanyard to show the Cover's current rating.<br /> <br /> This came off of another idea where we'd give a player a keyring with colour-coded index cards with their powers, so they don't need to remember what their individual powers do and you can easily find what they need etc. during game. Anything to make it easy for players to use their cool things without slowing down the actual game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:09:43-07:00","id":581434,"title":"","content":"Sounds like this could be a lot of fun. I'd be hesitant of making the demon form be the default costume, though. That just seems like an impossible task to border on getting anything remotely resembling the description of demon forms in the books. <br /> <br /> I haven't LARPed Demon (which sounds amazing, by the way) but in my tabletop group, those with multiple covers have one or two that they favor. I'd have folks costume for the main cover and have a lanyard with picture in it of any supporting covers. In the Requiem LARP I ran years ago, we had little pins with colored beads attached symbolizing blood potency. Perhaps you could add some flat colorful bead to the inside of the lanyard that can serve as an easy way to see the cover rating along with the cover picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","name":"IceIX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T18:51:44-07:00","id":581798,"title":"","content":"Well, I know some very talented costumers. But by far, the usual approach I've seen (especially in Changeling!) is just key features. I'm not really one to dictate how one can costume as their character in the slightest.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'm thinking of beads/clips or something similar to show the rating.<br /> <br /> I also reckon I could have some fun by making up some lanyards specifically for Fa\u00e7ades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}